### =============================================================
### 1. LOGIN -> servicio-autenticacion :8083
###    (demo accounts: see servicio-autenticacion/src/main/resources/application.yml)
###    The "> {% ... %}" block saves the token in a variable (IntelliJ HTTP Client).
### =============================================================

### Login as ADMIN
POST http://localhost:8083/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@tienda.com", "password": "Admin123*" }

> {% client.global.set("tokenAdmin", response.body.token); %}

### Login as CLIENTE (Ana)
POST http://localhost:8083/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@correo.com", "password": "Cliente123*" }

> {% client.global.set("tokenCliente", response.body.token); %}

### Sign up a new customer (always role CLIENTE)
POST http://localhost:8083/api/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "Luis Pérez", "email": "luis@correo.com", "password": "clave-luis-2026" }

### Public key used by the other services to verify tokens
GET http://localhost:8083/.well-known/jwks.json

### =============================================================
### 2. COMMANDS (write side) -> servicio-comandos :8081 -> PostgreSQL
### =============================================================

### [CLIENTE] Buy: only WHAT to buy; WHO buys comes from the token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/pedidos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCliente}}

{ "calzadoId": 1, "cantidad": 1 }

### [CLIENTE] Cancel one of MY orders (403 if it belongs to someone else)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/pedidos/1/cancelar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCliente}}

### [CLIENTE] Try to register a shoe -> 403 Forbidden
POST http://localhost:8081/api/calzados
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCliente}}

{ "marca": "X", "modelo": "X", "categoria": "casual", "talla": 40, "color": "x", "precio": 1000, "stockInicial": 1 }

### [no token] Buy -> 401 Unauthorized
POST http://localhost:8081/api/pedidos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "calzadoId": 1, "cantidad": 1 }

### [ADMIN] Register a shoe
POST http://localhost:8081/api/calzados
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

{ "marca": "Nike", "modelo": "Pegasus 41", "categoria": "deportivo", "talla": 41, "color": "negro", "precio": 529900, "stockInicial": 4 }

### [ADMIN] Change the price of shoe #1
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/calzados/1/precio
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

{ "nuevoPrecio": 399900 }

### [ADMIN] Restock shoe #7
POST http://localhost:8081/api/calzados/7/reponer-stock
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

{ "cantidad": 5 }

### [ADMIN] Ship order #1
POST http://localhost:8081/api/pedidos/1/despachar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

### =============================================================
### 3. QUERIES (read side) -> servicio-consultas :8082 -> MongoDB
### =============================================================

### [public] Catalog with filters
GET http://localhost:8082/api/catalogo?categoria=deportivo&precioMax=450000&soloDisponibles=true

### [CLIENTE] My orders (the e-mail comes from the token)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/pedidos/mios
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCliente}}

### [CLIENTE] All orders -> 403
GET http://localhost:8082/api/pedidos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCliente}}

### [ADMIN] All orders
GET http://localhost:8082/api/pedidos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

### [ADMIN] Rebuild the read model from the Kafka events
POST http://localhost:8082/api/admin/reconstruir
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
